      "content": "but sitting and waiting feels like a joke. i've been sitting in the dark for ages and the fog isn't lifting, it's just getting thicker. the cliff isn't even scary anymore, it actually looks... peaceful. like it's the only thing that's real anymore. the idea of just stepping out into that quiet void feels much more natural than trying to fight through this heaviness.",
